repository-code: "https://github.com/erenup/asymptotic-rank-sublevels"
abstract: >-
  Over the complex numbers, the set of tensors of asymptotic rank at most
  the cube root of 62 in format (3,3,3,2) is reducible in the Zariski
  topology. This answers the irreducibility assertion over all tensor
  orders negatively; the order-three question remains open. More
  generally, for every order k >= 4 with all factor dimensions at least
  two, every n >= 3 and every threshold a
  with B_n <= a < n+1, where n < B_n < n+1 is explicit, the sublevel has
  at least binomial(t_n,3)+1 irreducible components, with t_n the number
  of factors of dimension at least n.
  Includes the paper, plain-text proofs, exact supporting
  checks, and a Lean proof of the finite certificate layer. Files outside
  paper/ are licensed under MIT; files in paper/, including the manuscript
  source and PDF, are licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0.
